  {
   "id": "KBXMhf7dUIQJ",
   "from": "Dennis Murphy",
   "author": "0c39e60ddb38622b",
   "date": "2012-04-19T15:15:14Z",
   "subject": "Re: Question on a simple plot",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Manuel:<p>geom_step() is your friend here. Try this:<p></p></p>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<p><p>x &lt;- c(0,235,280,365)<br>y &lt;- c(1,0.94,0.89,0.89)<br>li &lt;- c(1,0.85,0.77,0.77)<br>ls &lt;- c(1,1,1,1)</p></p>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<p><p><p>DF &lt;- data.frame(x = x, y = y, li = li, ls = ls)<br>library(&#39;ggplot2&#39;)<br>ggplot(DF, aes(x = x)) +<br>    geom_step(aes(y = li), linetype = &#39;dashed&#39;) + geom_step(aes(y = y)) +<br>    geom_step(aes(y = ls), linetype = &#39;dashed&#39;) +  ylim(0, 1)<p>Dennis<p></p></p></p></p></p>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<p><p><p><p><p>On Thu, Apr 19, 2012 at 6:41 AM, Manuel Spínola &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mspin...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>&gt; Dear list members,<br>&gt;<br>&gt; How can I produce this plot in ggplot2 (I am thinking in the &quot;s&quot; argument,<br>&gt; how can be done in ggplot2)?<br>&gt;<br>&gt; x &lt;- c(0,235,280,365)<br>&gt; y &lt;- c(1,0.94,0.89,0.89)<br>&gt; li &lt;- c(1,0.85,0.77,0.77)<br>&gt; ls &lt;- c(1,1,1,1)<br>&gt;<br>&gt;<br>&gt; plot(x,y,type=&quot;s&quot;,ylim=c(0,1))<br>&gt; lines(x,li,type=&quot;s&quot;,lty=2)<br>&gt; lines(x,ls,type=&quot;s&quot;,lty=2)<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Best,<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Manuel<br>&gt;<br>&gt; --<br>&gt; Manuel Spínola, Ph.D.<br>&gt; Instituto Internacional en Conservación y Manejo de Vida Silvestre<br>&gt; Universidad Nacional<br>&gt; Apartado 1350-3000<br>&gt; Heredia<br>&gt; COSTA RICA<br>&gt; <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mspi...@una.ac.cr</a><br>&gt; <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mspin...@gmail.com</a><br>&gt; Teléfono: (506) 2277-3598<br>&gt; Fax: (506) 2237-7036<br>&gt; Personal website: Lobito de río<br>&gt; Institutional website: ICOMVIS<br>&gt;<br></p></p></p></p></p>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<p><p><p><p><p>&gt; --<br>&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing<br>&gt; list.<br>&gt; Please provide a reproducible example:<br>&gt; <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792376114155000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2SKrs929mo-3goRomkXYxS\">https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility</a><br>&gt;<br>&gt; To post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>&gt; To unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>&gt; More options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792376114155000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0y7qpxtT-TIeLt99--O3Ph\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a><br></p></p></p></p></p>"
